// A recipe. This page is its source: edit it here.
page RecipeShowCode(path: "/recipes/show-code", title: "Show code on a page — Recipes", description: "Show code on a page: inline in a sentence with Code, or as a block with CodeBlock, coloured by its language — wf, json, bash or css.") {
    RecipeShell("Show code on a page", summary: "`Code` shows code inline inside a sentence, and `CodeBlock` as a block, each coloured by its language. This page mixes inline code into a sentence and shows two coloured blocks:", outputs: ["website", "app", "pdf", "slides", "elements", "desktop"], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works")], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Describe pages to search engines and link previews", to: "/recipes/search-and-link-previews"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Pre-render a page for each item", to: "/recipes/pre-render-each-item"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Show your own page for an unknown address", to: "/recipes/not-found-page")], source: "site/src/pages/recipes/RecipeShowCode.wf", how: true, hasVariations: false, project: { "src/pages/ShowCode.wf": #"page Snippets(path: "/", title: "Snippets", description: "Code on the page.") {
    Heading("Snippets").h1
    Text("Run ")  Code("wf serve")  Text(" to start.")
    CodeBlock("page Home(path: \"/\") {\n    Text(\"Hi\")\n}", language: "wf")
    CodeBlock("$ wf build", language: "bash")
}
"#, "webfluent.app.json": #"{
  "name": "show-code"
}
"# }) {
        code {
            Markdown("**Needs:** nothing besides the page. It claims `/`: paste it into a new project, or replace the starter's `src/pages/Home.wf` with it.")
            DocsCodeBlock(#"page Snippets(path: "/", title: "Snippets", description: "Code on the page.") {
    Heading("Snippets").h1
    Text("Run ")  Code("wf serve")  Text(" to start.")
    CodeBlock("page Home(path: \"/\") {\n    Text(\"Hi\")\n}", language: "wf")
    CodeBlock("$ wf build", language: "bash")
}"#, title: "wf")
        }
        Markdown("- **`Code(\"…\")`** is inline code. Placed between two `Text`s, it reads as part of the sentence.\n- **`CodeBlock(\"…\")`** is a block, for code over several lines; `title:`, `.copy` and `.lines` add a bar with the file name, a copy button and line numbers.\n- **`language:`** colours it — `wf`, `json`, `bash` or `css`. The colouring is done at build time and in the browser alike, with the theme's `syntax-*` tokens, and a `Markdown` fence in one of those languages is coloured the same way.")

    }
}
